.TITLE "echo"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays messages or turns command echoing on or off. it is primarily used in __batch scripts__ to provide feedback to the user or to output text to a file.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**echo message**
Displays the specified text message in the console.
> __message__ the text to display

**echo off**
Prevents commands from being displayed as they are executed in a batch file.
> 

**echo %variable%**
Displays the value of a specific environment variable.
> __%variable%__ the target variable

**echo text > file.txt**
Writes the specified text to a file, overwriting its current contents.
> __>__ redirection operator | __file.txt__ the target file

**echo text >> file.txt**
Appends the specified text to the end of an existing file.
> __>>__ append operator

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Start your batch files with **@echo off** to prevent the script from displaying every command it runs, resulting in a cleaner output for the user. Using __echo.__ prints a blank line.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:set** **windows:type**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/echo__
